<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39131" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίδειξις</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίδεξις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>showing forth, making known</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦτο ἐς ἐ. ἀνθρώπων ἀπίκετο</span>
			became <i>notorious</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.46
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>.
				<i>exhibition</i>, <i>display, demonstration</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς δυνάμεως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					6.31
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ποιεῖσθαι</span>, of a
			military <i>demonstration</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				3.16
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἓν τοῦτ᾽ ἦν τῆς ἐ</span>.
				<i>showing off</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Grg.</u>
				447c
			</span></i>: generally, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ποιήσασθαι ᾗ . . </span>
			<i>exhibit</i> how . . , <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Phd.</u>
				99d
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλθεῖν εἰς ἐπίδειξίν
			τινι</span> come to <i>display</i> oneself to one, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				269
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ ἐ</span>. (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ κάλλους</span>) <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Mem.</u>
				3.11.2
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ποιήσασθαι τῆς σοφίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pol.</u>
					1259a19
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>. esp. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγων ἐ. ποιεῖσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					18.280
				</span></i>
			: abs., <i>set speech</i>, <i>declamation</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				3.42
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. ποιήσασθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Grg.</u>
					447c
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				4.17
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				5.17
			</span></i>: pl., <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				577.53
			</span></i> (Milet., <span class="entity">iii/ii B.C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				775.3
			</span></i> (Delph., <span class="entity">i B.C.</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>. name of a trireme at Athens, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				22.1623.144
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>.
			<i>proof</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				161.2
			</span></i> (pl.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>PTaur.</u>
				1.1
			</span></i><i><span class="en">
				 vii 7
			</span></i> (pl., <span class="entity">ii B.C.</span>), etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>. <i>example</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίδειξις Ἑλλάδι</span>
			<i>an example</i> to Greece, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				871
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίδειξιν ποιεῖσθαί τινι ὡς . . </span>
			<i>give a</i>
			<i>sign</i> or <i>proof</i> that . . , <i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				1.47
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
